From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:53:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] list only the keys a V4L2 camera honours

The template lists, for every camera, the keys of a camera with every
feature. A camera that lacks a feature then lists keys it cannot honour,
and CTS reads that as a contradiction:

- A camera without autofocus takes no AF region (maxRegions is 0 for it)
  and still listed android.control.afRegions as a request and a result
  key. StaticMetadataTest fails a camera that lists the key with no
  region.
- A camera without MANUAL_SENSOR listed android.sensor.frameDuration
  and android.blackLevel.lock, the sensor keys of that capability, so
  that it had every request key of MANUAL_SENSOR and every result key
  of READ_SENSOR_SETTINGS without listing either. StaticMetadataTest
  fails that as well.
- The tone map mode and the three curves were listed for every camera.
  A host camera makes its own picture and takes no curve, and CTS runs
  its tone map test for any camera that lists the mode, which then
  reads android.tonemap.maxCurvePoints, a number the HAL has no value
  for. No camera lists the four keys now, and none states
  android.tonemap.availableToneMapModes, which CameraDeviceTest wants
  listed together with the mode key. With no modes the templates carry
  no tone map key, and the camera is not refused for lacking them.

Take the keys that the camera's description does not earn out of both
lists, and the characteristic out of the metadata, from the rules in
camera_plan.hpp (unlisted_keys, unstated_characteristics), and state
the number of regions from the same place (max_regions_of). The tags
the rules name by number are asserted against camera_metadata_tags.h.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../hwl/EmulatedCameraDeviceInfo.cpp          |  5 ++++
 .../hwl/V4l2Characteristics.cpp               | 26 ++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/devices/EmulatedCamera/hwl/EmulatedCameraDeviceInfo.cpp b/devices/EmulatedCamera/hwl/EmulatedCameraDeviceInfo.cpp
index 4b21c5ab4e8f1c8239b35d0f90dcd0891c3848af..8738c6dd5eb4b33864e42b1e3d419f4fb622ae96 100644
--- a/devices/EmulatedCamera/hwl/EmulatedCameraDeviceInfo.cpp
+++ b/devices/EmulatedCamera/hwl/EmulatedCameraDeviceInfo.cpp
@@ -1203,6 +1203,11 @@ status_t EmulatedCameraDeviceInfo::InitializeTonemapDefaults() {
     if (ret == OK) {
       available_tonemap_modes_.insert(entry.data.u8,
                                       entry.data.u8 + entry.count);
+    } else if (!is_level_full_or_higher_) {
+      // A camera that states no tone map modes has no tone map control, and
+      // no template carries a tone map key: CTS wants the request key and
+      // the modes listed together.
+      return InitializeStatisticsDefaults();
     } else {
       ALOGE("%s: No available tonemap modes!", __FUNCTION__);
       return BAD_VALUE;
diff --git a/devices/EmulatedCamera/hwl/V4l2Characteristics.cpp b/devices/EmulatedCamera/hwl/V4l2Characteristics.cpp
index f4237ca777f78b4078eb9de9c868072a84daafec..b3fd28a51febec81356c5d87a45fcdaec86e6e89 100644
--- a/devices/EmulatedCamera/hwl/V4l2Characteristics.cpp
+++ b/devices/EmulatedCamera/hwl/V4l2Characteristics.cpp
@@ -44,6 +44,19 @@ namespace {
 namespace abi = andarium::camera::abi;
 namespace plan = andarium::camera;
 
+// camera_plan.hpp has no Android headers and states the tags of the keys it unlists by number.
+static_assert(plan::tag::control_ae_regions == ANDROID_CONTROL_AE_REGIONS);
+static_assert(plan::tag::control_af_regions == ANDROID_CONTROL_AF_REGIONS);
+static_assert(plan::tag::control_awb_regions == ANDROID_CONTROL_AWB_REGIONS);
+static_assert(plan::tag::sensor_frame_duration == ANDROID_SENSOR_FRAME_DURATION);
+static_assert(plan::tag::black_level_lock == ANDROID_BLACK_LEVEL_LOCK);
+static_assert(plan::tag::tonemap_curve_blue == ANDROID_TONEMAP_CURVE_BLUE);
+static_assert(plan::tag::tonemap_curve_green == ANDROID_TONEMAP_CURVE_GREEN);
+static_assert(plan::tag::tonemap_curve_red == ANDROID_TONEMAP_CURVE_RED);
+static_assert(plan::tag::tonemap_mode == ANDROID_TONEMAP_MODE);
+static_assert(plan::tag::tonemap_available_tone_map_modes ==
+              ANDROID_TONEMAP_AVAILABLE_TONE_MAP_MODES);
+
 constexpr char kTemplateFile[] = "emu_camera_v4l2.json";
 
 template <typename T>
@@ -286,7 +299,18 @@ status_t Specialize(const v4l2cam::CameraNodes& nodes, HalCameraMetadata* m) {
   } else {
     Put<uint8_t>(m, ANDROID_CONTROL_AF_AVAILABLE_MODES, {ANDROID_CONTROL_AF_MODE_OFF});
   }
-  Put<int32_t>(m, ANDROID_CONTROL_MAX_REGIONS, {1, 0, has_af ? 1 : 0});
+  const auto regions = plan::max_regions_of(desc);
+  Put<int32_t>(m, ANDROID_CONTROL_MAX_REGIONS, {regions[0], regions[1], regions[2]});
+  // The template lists the keys of a camera with every feature; this one lists only the keys it honours.
+  const std::vector<int32_t> keys = plan::unlisted_keys(desc, caps);
+  const std::set<int32_t> unlisted(keys.begin(), keys.end());
+  EditKeyList(m, ANDROID_REQUEST_AVAILABLE_REQUEST_KEYS, unlisted, {});
+  EditKeyList(m, ANDROID_REQUEST_AVAILABLE_RESULT_KEYS, unlisted, {});
+  // The modes are the other half of the tone map mode key: CTS wants the key and the modes listed together,
+  // so a camera that lists no mode states no modes (and the templates carry no tone map key).
+  for (const int32_t tag : plan::unstated_characteristics()) {
+    RemoveCharacteristic(m, static_cast<uint32_t>(tag));
+  }
 
   if (caps.manual_sensor) {
     Put<uint8_t>(m, ANDROID_CONTROL_AVAILABLE_MODES,
